Some of the early thoughts up on memories comes from Aristotle and he stated that humans were born free of any knowledge and are just sums of their own experiences. Those memories of personal experiences are called episodic memories and are very much connected certain evens or happenings that we as humans live through. Those memories are in turn captured as links or pathways in a part of our brain called hippocampus and is also here memories get connected together to be able to recall memories in a more holistic way.
Memories of personal experiences are called episodic memories and are captured in the part of the brain called hippocampus.
Episodic memories are captured in a part of the brain called the hippocampus.
When you can’t forget your childhood trauma, blame it in the hippocampus. The hippocampus never forgets. Hippocampus; helps you remember. Thing deep, think Hippocampus. The dark side; Hippocampus. Hippocampus forms you. A form for you; Hippocampus. Re-form Hippocampus. A long time ago; Hippocampus links it up! Bring it back Hippocampus. Hippocampus rules you! I am not me, I am my Hippocampus. Hippocampus; what you want to forget in the future. Futures worst enemy: Hippocampus. Forgiveness worst enemy; Hippocampus. I am how I am. Thank you Hippocampus.
