<|asst|>
Type II diabetes is 90% cases of diabetes. If you have diabetes you should speak to your physician about getting on a strict diet, exercise and medications. Complications of diabetes are cardiovascular, kidney disease and nerve damage. Type II diabetes generally occurs in people over 40. You should manage your weight, quit smoking, exercise regularly, limit or avoid processed foods and limit your alcohol intake to help reduce your risk of type II diabetes.
<|end|>


