The Grand Comoro Drongo (Dicrurus fuscipennis) is a species of bird in the Dicruridae family. It is endemic to Comoros.
Its natural habitats are subtropical or tropical moist lowland forests, pastureland, and plantations. It is threatened by habitat loss.
- BirdLife International 2004. Dicrurus fuscipennis. 2006 IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. Downloaded on 25 July 2007.
