who was angel moroni
Angel Moroni is a figure who appears in the religious text of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS). Moroni is said to be an angel who visited Joseph Smith, the founder of the LDS Church, and gave him a set of golden plates which contained the religious text that would later be known as the Book of Mormon.
why did he visit joseph smith
Although we don’t know for sure why the angel Moroni visited Joseph Smith, it is believed that he came to give Joseph Smith a message from God. It is possible that the angel Moroni was also trying to prepare Joseph Smith for the great work that he would need to do in bringing forth the gospel of Jesus Christ.
what did he tell joseph smith
The Angel Moroni is an angel who, according to Latter Day Saint belief, visited Joseph Smith on numerous occasions, beginning on September 21, 1823. An important figure in the early history of the Latter Day Saint movement, Moroni is featured prominently in the religion’s origin story.
On the evening of September 21, 1823, Smith said that he was visited in his bedroom by a “personage” who identified himself as the “Angel Moroni.” According to Smith’s account, Moroni informed him about a book made of golden plates that was buried in a nearby hill; this record contained “the fulness of the everlasting Gospel” and would be useful in restoring Christianity to its former purity.
how did this event change joseph smith’s life
On September 21, 1823, Joseph Smith claimed to have received a visit from an angel named Moroni. This event changed his life forever. Moroni told him about a sacred text that was buried in a nearby hill. This text, the Book of Mormon, would later be published and become an important part of the LDS religion.
